\]
Now, we use the addition formula for tangent to find $ \tan 3\theta = \tan (2\theta + \theta) $: \[
\tan 3\theta = \tan (2\theta + \theta) = \frac{\tan 2\theta + \tan \theta}{1 - \tan 2\theta \tan \theta}
\]
Substituting $ \tan 2\theta = -\frac{8}{15} $ and $ \tan \theta = 4 $ into the formula, we get: \[
